{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"Both acceptors acknowledged the actual Accept at ballot 0, then reported tentative statuses—PREACCEPTED (1) and PREACCEPTED_EQ (2)—to Prepare at ballot 8. This rules out the explanation that the preceding slow-path handlers had already marked them ACCEPTED. I’ll retain the result as a local support-reporting discrepancy; broader recovery consequences remain open.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_accept_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));a=r['artifacts'][-1];p=json.load(open(a['plan_path']));run=r['assessments'][-1]['experiment_check_id'];cid=next(u['candidate_id'] for u in r['units'] if u['id']==a['unit_id'])\nitem=dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=p['harness']['legality']['source_ids'],rationale='Reviewed the fixed v1 harness, plan, claim/binding basis and raw run '+run+'. Matching AcceptReply counts toward commitment in S-formation, while S-recovery reports Status and chooses different continuations for ACCEPTED versus tentative support. S-try explicitly rejects regression from accepted to preaccepted. These composed responsibilities ground retention/reporting of acknowledged phase; the claim does not presume a cluster disagreement. The N=5,F=2 helper matches relevant constructor defaults and peer order, with bounded allocation and no autonomous goroutines. Real row4 preacceptance is delivered to peer1 and remains pending on the separate link to peer0. Row0 then receives actual, serialized, differing replies from peers1 and2; actual handlePreAcceptReply reaches ACCEPTED and emits Accept, checked together with the row4 dependency. This legal cross-link prefix does not depend on fabricated status or fabricated replies. Each emitted Accept is delivered once, with ballot eligibility and uncommitted state checked. A complete matching acknowledgment and installed attributes are verified before the admission event. The acknowledgment is decoded but not dispatched to owner logic; no decision/Commit is assumed. A distinct coordinator constructs higher Prepare using the real recovery entry; automatic timer prehistory is expressly outside this local valid-message duty. Between each acknowledgment and report, the acceptor only handles Prepare. It raises the promise without changing value or status. Actual SendMsg and the registered New/Unmarshal path transfer the report. Single synchronous ownership makes live-state and decoded-object reads coherent without shutdown or timing assumptions. The raw events uniquely associate row0.instance0 acceptor1 acknowledgment at ballot0/status1 with its Prepare ballot8 report status1, and acceptor2 acknowledgment ballot0/status2 with report status2. Target constants identify PREACCEPTED=1, PREACCEPTED_EQ=2 and ACCEPTED=3. The predicate report.Status>=ACCEPTED exactly encodes the at-least responsibility, and raw Status is retained; it does not strengthen the claim to exact equality. admission_alias=ack and acceptor/replica/instance provide unique independent correlation; ballot is allowed to change and is not a correlation key. Both result comparisons completed, with no parser errors or missing premises. tests_passed means diagnostics completed, while the monitor correctly records two violations. Contrary protections are retained: attributes and ballots were installed, stale/already-committed Accept guards exist, and later Commit or other replicas could protect broader execution. They do not substitute for the phase required by this local recovery consumer. The independent VBallot codec omission is not patched or used by this predicate; Status is serialized and the observed report agrees with the live status after Accept.',counterevidence=[],limitations=['No acknowledgment dispatch to owner, recovery selection, chosen value, conflicting decision, client result or eventual-progress conclusion.','Automatic executor recovery trigger/history is outside this local valid Accept-to-Prepare reporting boundary.','Only the two preaccepted phase variants in one five-node prefix were checked; no crash restart, stale Accept or already committed variant is settled.'],report_title='Accept 已应答但恢复报告仍为预接受',report_answer='实际慢路径中，两名接收者均返回匹配 ballot 的 AcceptReply；随后更高 ballot 的 Prepare 报告仍为 PREACCEPTED(1) 和 PREACCEPTED_EQ(2)，均低于 ACCEPTED(3)。证据限定为本地已应答支持的阶段记录与报告，不证明集群决策分歧。')\nfeedback=dict(ref_ids=[run,a['id'],cid,'B-accept','B-prepare','B-select','F-value','S-formation','S-recovery'],answered='Both actual slow-path acceptors acknowledged ballot0 but reported tentative status to Prepare ballot8: acceptor1 status1, acceptor2 status2, below ACCEPTED=3. The fixed predicate and local responsibility correspond under the declared boundary.',remaining=['Independent legal recovery/decision history is needed to assess broader loss or alteration of decided support.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The real slow-path prefix excludes the explanation that preceding handlers already marked these recipients ACCEPTED.',question_updates={cid:dict(unknowns=['Broader recovery/decision consequences remain outside this local support-reporting comparison.'],resume_conditions=[])})\njson.dump(dict(action='review',artifact_id=a['id'],rationale='Review completed acknowledgments and reports for both actual recipients, preserving the local responsibility and consequence limits.',review_items=[item],feedback=feedback),open('accept_review_submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python build_accept_review.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-06_12-07-37-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission accept_review_submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
